From 104ffb37573209746ce7058d901686cfa944d016 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Rajan <7121943+kvnloo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 20:31:14 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] docs(skills): use the questions=[...] clarify shape; drop
 single-choice limits

The clarify tool takes one argument, `questions` - a list of
{question, choices?, multi_select?} entries (tools/clarify_tool.py). The
pixel-art skill still showed the old top-level
`clarify(question=..., choices=...)` form, which the tool rejects with
"questions must be a non-empty array. Pass questions=[{question, choices?,
multi_select?}]". The openclaw-migration skill still said the CLI handles
"one choice at a time" and has no multi-select, but clarify takes several
questions per call and `multi_select: true` renders checkbox rows in the
CLI panel (hermes_cli/cli_modal_mixin.py, cli_tui_mixin.py).

- pixel-art SKILL.md: both examples moved to `clarify(questions=[{...}])`.
- openclaw-migration SKILL.md: drop the two false limits.
- website per-skill pages regenerated with website/scripts/generate-skill-docs.py
  (only these two pages change).
- zh-Hans openclaw-migration page (hand-translated, not regenerated): same
  two lines dropped, and its retry hint now names the `questions` array as
  the English source already does.
